1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,115
Meet Brix, a friendly data assistant living in a bakery.

2
00:00:04,165 --> 00:00:09,911
It runs as a Databricks App and answers from a Genie agent over your Bakehouse data.

3
00:00:12,084 --> 00:00:14,626
When it's quiet, Brix vibes to music.

4
00:00:14,676 --> 00:00:18,479
Click to play or pause, double-click for the next song.

5
00:00:18,529 --> 00:00:21,001
The TV in the counter is the player.

6
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:30,778
The window follows your clock: the sun and moon move, the moon shows its real phase, and the weather is local.

7
00:00:40,254 --> 00:00:45,124
The chalkboard shows live revenue and top customers from your dashboard.

8
00:00:45,174 --> 00:00:46,900
Tap it to open dashboards.

9
00:00:53,174 --> 00:00:58,979
The tickets are the last three runs of the daily job, and the oven light shows pipeline health.

10
00:00:59,958 --> 00:01:03,907
The recipe book is your catalog, with each table's freshness.

11
00:01:06,051 --> 00:01:07,996
Ask anything in plain English.

12
00:01:08,046 --> 00:01:13,913
Brix acts out what Genie is doing: finding data, planning the query, running the numbers.

13
00:01:14,016 --> 00:01:20,574
Brix: Here is the daily revenue for the last 30 days; this period falls in Oct 25, 2026 to Nov 23, 2026, which is simulated test data rather than real business activity.

14
00:01:20,624 --> 00:01:21,993
Brix: Examples include: October 25: 4260.

15
00:01:22,143 --> 00:01:25,430
Answers come with a chart, or switch to the table.

16
00:01:27,597 --> 00:01:31,503
Pull the lamp chain to dim the room, and the panels go dark.

17
00:01:35,041 --> 00:01:39,161
If the daily job fails, Brix tells you, with a link to the run.

18
00:01:40,012 --> 00:01:45,454
The menu lists everything you can ask or do, including hands-free chat with the mic.

19
00:01:46,305 --> 00:01:51,781
Each croissant is someone here right now, and the counter shows everyone served.

20
00:01:51,831 --> 00:01:52,610
That's Brix!
